Fixed the viewport meta tag disabling pinch-zoom and text scaling, which prevented users from magnifying any page (WCAG 1.4.4).
Fixed icon-only footer links, panel collapse toggles, the actions dropdown, the per-page selector, object list row checkboxes and unlabelled textareas having no accessible name.
Fixed job approval actions, help and documentation buttons, dropdown toggles, cable trace links, image attachment and service actions, and the App Marketplace docs links having no accessible name.
Fixed the "toggle all rows" table checkbox lacking an accessible name and not reflecting partial selection, contradictory attributes on the decorative page title chevron, and a missing `lang` attribute on the GraphiQL page.
Fixed the "Items per page" control on the theme preview page having no accessible name.
Fixed form field help text and validation errors not being announced by screen readers, by giving them the element IDs that Django's generated `aria-describedby` attribute already pointed at.
Fixed heading levels being skipped, and added a heading to the home page, so that heading-based navigation reflects page structure.
Fixed home page panels emitting `<div>` children directly inside a `<ul>`, which stopped them being reported as lists, and fixed job history entries rendering an empty link when the underlying Job record no longer exists.
Fixed modal dialogs having no accessible name by adding `aria-labelledby`, `aria-modal` and `role="dialog"` to all modals.
Fixed data table accessibility by adding `scope="col"` to table headers, exposing sort state via `aria-sort`, giving each table a visually hidden `<caption>`, and correcting invalid self-closing `<td />` markup.
Fixed the bulk-action controls on object list views remaining reachable by keyboard and announced by screen readers while visually hidden.
Fixed images missing `alt` attributes.
Fixed the header search input and the search popup input having no accessible name, which was lost when the typeahead placeholder replaced it.
Fixed touch targets below the WCAG 2.5.8 minimum size: the header search-help link and the tree expand carets are padded up to 24px without shifting the layout, and the actions column on embedded detail-page tables no longer renders a sort link, which was also a broken URL.
Fixed Select2 fields having no accessible name by pointing the rendered widget's `aria-labelledby` at the field's form labels, which Select2 otherwise names after their own displayed value.
Fixed submitting the Location create form without a Location Type raising `RelatedObjectDoesNotExist` from `Location.clean()` instead of reporting the field as required.
